  "kind": "standard",
  "confidence": "medium",
  "drawnOn": "A20N",
  "description": "White aircraft with 'SKY' in big navy capitals and 'express' in thin navy lower case under it on the forward fuselage, and 'Greece is bliss' in navy under the rear windows. The tail is a set of upright stripes: navy bars on the white fin, from its leading edge up, with a navy cap along the tip, and magenta bars beside and under them that run on down the rear fuselage nearly to the belly, each starting lower toward the front, so the stripes step down the tail like a stair. Navy engines with 'skyexpress.gr' in white; magenta winglets.",
  "sources": [
    {
      "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Hannover_Airport_SKY_express_Airbus_A320-251N_SX-TEC_(DSC01680).jpg",
      "title": "Hannover Airport SKY express Airbus A320-251N SX-TEC (DSC01680) (CC BY-SA 4.0, MarcelX42)",
      "accessed": "2026-11-21",
      "note": "A320neo SX-TEC taxiing at Hannover, left side, level, 2021-10-09. Fitted to shapes/A20N.json (doors pinned, within 5 px): every tail stripe read column by column off the photo (navy and magenta against white, the magenta in the stabilizer's shadow too) and converted to fuselage and fin space; the titles' ends and heights."
    },
    {
      "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Hannover_Airport_SKY_express_Airbus_A320-251N_SX-TEC_(DSC01795).jpg",
