  "notes": "Measured on SX-TEC (A320neo, left side, Hannover, 2021-10-09), fitted to the A320neo shape; still worn in 2026. The tail's stripes were read off the photo column by column and each bar drawn as its pixel outline converted to fuselage and fin space (straight edges: the bars are upright in a side view, so slanted in fin space, which is sheared). Seven navy bars about 0.45 m wide at a pitch of about 1 m, from the fin's leading edge up (the aft ones from the navy cap at the tip), their feet stepping up toward the tail (from about 0.7 m above the centreline at the front to the fin's middle at the back); eight magenta bars, each overlapping its navy bar's aft half from part way down and running on nearly to the belly, the first two (behind the aft door) only on the lower fuselage. Under the tailplane the magenta is in shadow; its foot was read there with a looser colour test. Fine detail is simplified: on the aircraft a thin white diagonal separates each navy bar's foot from the magenta. The right side is assumed to match (the stripes are upright, so the fin is drawn mirrored). The belly isn't seen. SKY express's A321neos and ATRs wear the same scheme.",
  "history": "New 2026-11-21 (the maintainer's sightings: SX-TEC)."
}
